<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-5061] User notebook information is leaked through home page</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-5061</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Steps to reproduce:&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Have at least two users and two browser sessions simultaneously, users A and B&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;User A creates a notebook and navigates to the home page.&#160; Their notebook will display&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;User B creates a notebook and navigates to the home page.&#160; Their notebook will display&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;However, in User A&apos;s browser session, User B&apos;s notebook will display.&#160;&#160;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Note that notebook sharing is disabled.&#160; This seems to be like some global state that websockets is mistakely updating.&#160; More than that I haven&apos;t determined&lt;/p&gt;</description>
